      "writtenOn": "2026-10-29T16:31:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Follow-up (verify / --validate-env): speed drift is checked by exact full-line match of the command-form token from expected_speed_statement (e.g. \u0027speed forced 10gfull\u0027, \u0027speed auto 100g-2\u0027) against `show running-config interfaces` output. If EOS renders the stored token differently (e.g. \u0027speed forced 10000full\u0027), a correctly configured Arista port reports false speed drift: without --change verify returns False for the host; with --change it needlessly re-applies the port (and re-runs convert_port_public on the public NIC). The driver _set_speed matches tolerantly (regex), but this plugin-side check is exact, and the tests feed the sent token back as running-config so they cannot catch a canonicalization mismatch. No Juniper precedent (Juniper verify never checks speed). Please confirm against a real `show running-config interfaces` capture per speed (1/10/25/40/100G) on the POC EOS.",
      "revId": "751fd0b8ddbd8c77061da27dd195a130e3b4d606",
