      "side": 1,
      "message": "Fixed in PS21: verify() no longer compares the raw command-form token. The running-config lines are parsed to (mode, Mbps) via speed_statement_matches(), so EOS renderings such as \u0027speed forced 10000full\u0027 (for the sent \u0027speed forced 10gfull\u0027) and the 100g-2 auto form compare equal; a genuine mismatch still fails closed and --change still re-applies. Added matcher unit tests and a plugin verify test that returns the canonicalized token. I could not capture running-config from the POC switch in this environment (no EOS credentials here), but the comparison is now independent of the rendered token form.",
