      "writtenOn": "2026-10-29T16:31:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Follow-up (by-design, mixed-vendor only): configure short-circuits on the first plugin whose result is not True. If plugin A commits real VLAN changes on its switch and plugin B then fails, the dispatcher returns False and the move loop drops the host, leaving it with one switch reconfigured to the new cloud while it stays in the old cloud until a retry re-runs configure (self-healing; already-correct ports are skipped). Inherent to non-atomic multi-switch config; it does not affect single-plugin (Juniper-only) deployments. Noting for awareness.",
      "revId": "751fd0b8ddbd8c77061da27dd195a130e3b4d606",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
