      "writtenOn": "2026-10-29T16:31:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Blocking: this new nullable_string_keys path (include \u003d key in data) clears vendor and switch_vendor whenever the PATCH body carries them as null. The CLI always carries them: --interface-vendor / --interface-switch-vendor use default\u003dNone (parser.py:641-653), main.py does vars(parse_args()), and action_modinterface (cli.py:2036-2038) copies every present key, so a mod that touches only e.g. speed sends vendor\u003dnull and switch_vendor\u003dnull and both are wiped. dev-parent used bool(value), so None was ignored and vendor was preserved; this is a regression. Reproduced: `--mod-interface --interface-speed 10` builds setattr {\u0027speed\u0027,\u0027vendor\u0027:None,\u0027switch_vendor\u0027:None}. It destroys the pre-existing vendor field and silently reverts the switch_vendor routing tag (an Arista port becomes unclaimed; a mixed site has Juniper try to program an Arista switch), and it triggers on this change\u0027s own advice to --mod-interface speeds before moving Arista hosts. Minimal fix: default\u003dargparse.SUPPRESS on both args (matches --pxe-boot / --maintenance); clearing via \u0027\u0027 or an API null still works. No test covers this; please add one that PATCHes an unrelated field and asserts vendor / switch_vendor survive.",
      "revId": "751fd0b8ddbd8c77061da27dd195a130e3b4d606",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
